  "**OneUptime AI agent (on by default, read-only).** AI investigations are on: with the install script or Docker Compose, the OneUptime AI agent runs beside the collector and lets OneUptime AI read this database's diagnostics while it investigates an incident or alert, and it changes nothing unless you allow fixes — see **The files the agent runs** under Advanced.":
    "**OneUptime AI-agent (slået til som standard, skrivebeskyttet).** AI-undersøgelser er slået til: med installationsscriptet eller Docker Compose kører OneUptime AI-agenten ved siden af collectoren og lader OneUptime AI læse denne databases diagnostik, mens den undersøger en hændelse eller en alarm, og den ændrer intet, medmindre du tillader rettelser — se **De filer, agenten kører** under Avanceret.",
  "The OneUptime Database Agent collects PostgreSQL engine metrics — connections against `max_connections`, commits and rollbacks, cache hit ratio, row throughput, locks and deadlocks, temporary files, database, table and index sizes, checkpoints and the background writer, vacuums and replication lag, plus optional query samples and top queries (`DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS`) — with a stock OpenTelemetry Collector container (`otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.161.0`) running the collector's native `postgresql` receiver (`configs/postgresql.yaml`). Nothing is installed on the database server. **One agent monitors one database server**; run a second copy in a second directory for a second server.":
    "OneUptime Database Agent indsamler engine-metrikker for PostgreSQL (forbindelser i forhold til `max_connections`, commits og rollbacks, cache-hitrate, rækkegennemløb, låse og deadlocks, midlertidige filer, størrelser på databaser, tabeller og indeks, checkpoints og background writer, vacuums og replikeringsforsinkelse samt valgfrie forespørgselseksempler og topforespørgsler (`DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS`)) med en standardcontainer med OpenTelemetry Collector (`otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.161.0`), der kører collectorens indbyggede `postgresql`-receiver (`configs/postgresql.yaml`). Der installeres intet på databaseserveren. **Én agent overvåger én databaseserver**; kør en ekstra kopi i en ekstra mappe til en ekstra server.",
  "With `DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS=true` the agent also ships query samples and top queries as logs: they arrive on the database's **Logs** tab with the query text as their message. They contain query text, so they are off by default — the install script asks whether to ship them.":
    "Med `DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS=true` sender agenten også forespørgselseksempler og topforespørgsler som protokoller: de ankommer på databasens fane **Protokoller** med forespørgselsteksten som besked. De indeholder forespørgselstekst, så de er slået fra som standard — installationsscriptet spørger, om de skal sendes.",
  "To turn them on later, set `DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS=true` in the agent's `.env` and recreate the container with `docker compose up -d --force-recreate` in its folder.":
    "For at slå dem til senere skal du sætte `DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS=true` i agentens `.env` og genskabe containeren med `docker compose up -d --force-recreate` i dens mappe.",
  "Top queries (`DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS=true`) also need the `pg_stat_statements` extension, loaded through `shared_preload_libraries = 'pg_stat_statements'` (a restart) and created in every monitored database:":
    "Topforespørgsler (`DATABASE_QUERY_EVENTS=true`) kræver også udvidelsen `pg_stat_statements`, indlæst via `shared_preload_libraries = 'pg_stat_statements'` (en genstart) og oprettet i hver overvåget database:",
  "Their explain plans additionally need `SELECT` on the tables the queries touch, which `pg_monitor` does not grant (for example `GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA app TO oneuptime_monitor`). Without it top queries still arrive, with empty plans, and the collector logs `failed to explain` for each one.":
    "Deres udførelsesplaner kræver desuden `SELECT` på de tabeller, forespørgslerne rører, hvilket `pg_monitor` ikke giver (for eksempel `GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA app TO oneuptime_monitor`). Uden det ankommer topforespørgsler alligevel, med tomme planer, og collectoren logger `failed to explain` for hver af dem.",
